stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> IDLE
    IDLE --> PREFLIGHT: mission_request ∧ ground_task_complete
    PREFLIGHT --> ARMING: side_door_closed ∧ px4_ready
    ARMING --> TAKEOFF: armed ∧ offboard
    TAKEOFF --> EGO_TRANSIT: at_takeoff_pose (home.xz, takeoff_height)
    EGO_TRANSIT --> TARGET_SEARCH: at_search_pose (drop_search_pose)
    TARGET_SEARCH --> VISUAL_ALIGN: target_visible
    VISUAL_ALIGN --> DROP_HOLD: target_aligned (visual stable ≥ 0.8 s)
    DROP_HOLD --> RETURN: payload_released
    RETURN --> LAND: at_home
    LAND --> COMPLETE: landed

    state HOLD_EMERGENCY {
        [*] --> HOLD
        HOLD --> LAND: stale_data > 1.0 s OR px4_failsafe
    }
    ARMING --> HOLD_EMERGENCY: stale_data > 0.3 s
    TAKEOFF --> HOLD_EMERGENCY: stale_data > 0.3 s
    EGO_TRANSIT --> HOLD_EMERGENCY: stale_data > 0.3 s
    TARGET_SEARCH --> HOLD_EMERGENCY: stale_data > 0.3 s
    VISUAL_ALIGN --> HOLD_EMERGENCY: stale_data > 0.3 s
    DROP_HOLD --> HOLD_EMERGENCY: stale_data > 0.3 s
    RETURN --> HOLD_EMERGENCY: stale_data > 0.3 s
    HOLD_EMERGENCY --> LAND: emergency_land_sent

    note right of PREFLIGHT
        supervisor publishes "left_close" until
        /cargo_bay/status reports "left_closed" or
        "side_closed"; the request is idempotent.
    end note

    note right of DROP_HOLD
        supervisor publishes "bottom_open" once and
        waits for /cargo_bay/status to contain
        "payload_released".
    end note
